Consider the following C code snippet intended to insert a new node `newNode` at the head of a singly linked list with head pointer `head`:

```c
newNode->next = head;
head = newNode;
```

If a student mistakenly writes the code in the reverse order:

```c
head = newNode;
newNode->next = head;
```

What is the immediate consequence of this error on the linked list structure?
